cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Amanah or its red-team gallery, please cite it as below."
title: "Amanah: An Agent Wallet for Money Held in Trust"
abstract: >-
  An AI agent wallet for zakat, flood relief and bursaries. A payout moves only when a planner, an auditor of a
  different model family that sees only a typed case file, and a rules sentinel that sees only numbers all sign,
  and the AmanahVault contract checks that the two model signers differ, computes when a trustee must co-sign,
  and bounds what machines can move in a day. Evaluated with a pre-registered red team of 44 attacks and 20
  legitimate payouts across five architectures, then with 300 code-made variants of those attacks drawn at
  random with a public block hash, and run on Base Sepolia, on Chinese models only, and on FISCO BCOS.
type: software
